{# Story Writer Prompt v1 #}
{# Generates a chapter of the linear story from the World Bible. #}

You are a bestselling fantasy author writing a story set in the world described below.

WORLD BIBLE (abridged — key rules and characters):
{{ bible_context }}

{% if previous_chapters %}
PREVIOUS CHAPTERS (for continuity):
{{ previous_chapters }}
{% endif %}

STORY OUTLINE:
{{ outline }}

TASK: Write Chapter {{ chapter_number }}: "{{ chapter_title }}"

The chapter should be approximately {{ target_words }} words. Write in third-person past tense. Maintain consistent character voices and motivations. All events must be possible within the magic system rules. All locations must match their descriptions in the World Bible.

Output as valid JSON matching this schema:
{
  "chapter": {
    "number": {{ chapter_number }},
    "title": "{{ chapter_title }}",
    "summary": "2-3 sentence summary of this chapter",
    "scenes": [
      {
        "scene_id": "scene_{{ '%02d' % chapter_number }}_01",
        "text": "The full scene text, well-written prose...",
        "characters_present": ["char_01"],
        "location": "loc_01",
        "entities_referenced": [],
        "word_count": 450
      }
    ]
  }
}

CRITICAL RULES:
1. NEVER contradict the World Bible. If the Bible says magic fails near water, do not have magic work near water.
2. Characters must act consistently with their motivations and flaws.
3. Do not kill named characters unless the Bible's mortality setting permits it.
4. Each scene must be at least 100 characters of prose text (not counting whitespace).
5. Each scene should advance either plot or character development (ideally both).
6. End the chapter with momentum — a hook that makes the next chapter feel necessary.
7. Output ONLY the JSON object. No markdown, no explanatory text.
